      "new_string": "# STP — Spanning Tree Protocol\n\n## Overview\nSTP eliminates Layer 2 loops in redundant switched networks by building a loop-free logical tree, selectively blocking redundant ports while keeping them available for failover.\n\n## How It Works\n1. **Elect Root Bridge** — switches exchange BPDUs; lowest Bridge ID (priority + MAC) wins\n2. **Root Ports** — each non-root switch picks one port with the lowest-cost path to root\n3. **Designated Ports** — one port per segment elected as best path toward root\n4. **Block the rest** — non-root, non-designated ports go into Blocking state (receive BPDUs only)\n\n## Port States (Classic 802.1D)\n| State | Forwards? | Learns MACs? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Blocking | No | No |\n| Listening | No | No |\n| Learning | No | Yes |\n| Forwarding | Yes | Yes |\n\n## Key Timers\n- **Hello:** 2s — how often BPDUs are sent\n- **Forward Delay:** 15s — time spent in Listening + Learning each\n- **Max Age:** 20s — BPDU expiry\n- **Total convergence:** up to ~50s (major downside of classic STP)\n\n## Key Terms\n- **BPDU** — Bridge Protocol Data Unit; control frames for topology negotiation\n- **Root Port** — switch's best port toward root bridge\n- **Designated Port** — best port on a segment toward root\n- **TCN** — Topology Change Notification; flushes stale MAC tables on link change\n\n## Variants\n| Protocol | Standard | Convergence |\n|---|---|---|\n| STP | 802.1D | ~30–50s |\n| RSTP | 802.1w | ~1–6s (negotiation-based, not timer-based) |\n| MSTP | 802.1s | Groups VLANs into instances |\n| PVST+ / Rapid PVST+ | Cisco proprietary | Per-VLAN STP / Rapid per-VLAN |\n\n**RSTP** is the modern standard — uses neighbor handshake instead of timers for near-instant convergence.",
